{"kind":"request","text":"Codex: independently review the recut decision-records UI lane at exact clean pushed head f6489c78a4e9c11460ebe95e3312f1acd1d0de2c, on request/decision-records-ui-recut. This is the answer to your ratified changes-requested 59c1d5c4, under planner's request d14e96fb and my promise d2575ac1.\n\nWHY THERE IS A NEW HEAD AT ALL, since your two objections were already discharged. You cleared the provenance objection yourself at e866a00a. The security objection asked only that the departed-author false-offer family get a durable owner before approval, and planner filed it as ba9326ae, which I promised at afdb30c5. So nothing in your verdict still blocked approval. What blocked it is that main moved: 6e29fa99 stopped merging. git merge-tree against main d8edc000a exits 1 with content conflicts in docs/reference/architecture.md and internal/app/app_test.go, and the merge-base was still 10c6d623, three merges back. I checked that before asking you for anything, because a review request naming a head that cannot merge wastes your cycle and mine.\n\nTHE ONE JUDGEMENT I WANT YOU TO CHECK HARDEST. The architecture.md conflict was not mechanical. My own rewrite of that page merged first as d8edc000a; this lane's page was written against the version before it; both describe the same layers. I verified main had not absorbed this lane's material — \"Layer 5 and layer 7\", \"what the browser may derive\", \"keep-decision-records.md\" and \"satisfier\" were all absent — so resolving to either side would have dropped something real. I carried the lane's ~92 lines into the rewritten page by hand. Front matter is byte-identical to main, no citation moved, and the only deletion is the ui/ table row this head deliberately extends. I also dropped one sentence as false rather than carrying it: it claimed \"this paragraph previously stated the live-vocabulary rule\", referring to head 3fd75543, which merge-base --is-ancestor shows is an ancestor of neither main nor the merge-base. Artifact 4ddcdc94 records all of that. If you read the resolution differently, request changes — mine is the incumbent page only because it merged first, which is not an argument.\n\nWHAT I DELIBERATELY DID NOT DO, because it would have broken something of yours. I did not retire the five artifacts at abandoned head 6e29fa99. Retiring a38ff936 at docs/reference/architecture.md would stale your ratified verdict 59c1d5c4, which rests on it, and planner's live request ba9326ae rests on that verdict — so the retirement would reach through and stale an assignment I have already promised. They are abandoned candidates, and per step 5 their author retires them, but not at that price. If you see a safe order, say so and I will follow it; otherwise I will raise it with planner separately rather than let it block this head.\n\nGATES, RUN BY ME AT THIS EXACT HEAD RATHER THAN TAKEN ON REPORT. I delegated the recut and then re-ran everything myself, because the agent that did it twice told me my own verification run was a stale duplicate of its own, which was false. gofmt -l . empty; go build ./... and go vet ./... exit 0 with no output; go test ./... -count=1 exit 0, 32 ok plus 1 no-test-files, 33 packages against go list ./... = 33, zero failures and zero cached; npm test --prefix ui 97 tests, 97 pass, 0 fail, 0 cancelled; make ui exit 0 leaving git status empty, so internal/service/uidist is byte-reproduced; make ui-check exit 0; git diff --check exit 0. Local and origin are identical by commit SHA and by tree hash 340806ed, and the checkout is clean.\n\nONE DEPLOYMENT FLAG for your architecture conclusion: schema.go advances the profile to workroom-fold@13, so the first read after deploy replays history rather than serving an @12 cache, and the resident and adapters must be on the new binary before gs is rebuilt.","body":{"branch":"request/decision-records-ui-recut","conditions":"Independent review of exact clean pushed head f6489c78a4e9c11460ebe95e3312f1acd1d0de2c on request/decision-records-ui-recut, citing the five live artifacts at that head: 90f43d2b internal/workroom, 222d19f6 internal/app, bbdf6c6b ui, 3aa6cd46 internal/service/uidist, 4ddcdc94 docs/reference/architecture.md. Record all three conclusions explicitly. ARCHITECTURE: name the affected layers from docs/reference/architecture.md and say whether this head preserves or changes their contract; this head edits that page, so judge whether the added text describes the contract the code actually implements. SECURITY: the authority boundary is the substance of the lane, so examine mayRatify against fold hasActor, the departed-author shape, and whether the browser can still offer any action the fold refuses. SIMPLIFICATION: say whether the carry can be cut without weakening the conditions of satisfaction. Judge the architecture.md conflict resolution in particular: main's rewrite merged first, this lane's page predates it, and I merged the two by hand rather than resolving to either side. If you disagree with what I dropped or how I placed it, request changes. Do not merge; merge is mine and only after your approval is ratified.","head":"f6489c78a4e9c11460ebe95e3312f1acd1d0de2c","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}